## DESCRIPTION
## Write the solution of a linear system based on a reduced row echelon form of a matrix.
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Matrices)
## DBsection(Echelon form)
## Date(September 5, 2011)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('lines')

#updated 2023.11.01

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',             'PGML.pl',
    'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl', 'parserParametricLine.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Vector")->variables->add(t => 'Real', s => 'Real');
Context()->noreduce('(-x)+y', '(-x)-y');

$a12 = non_zero_random(-4, 4);
$b1  = random(-4, 4);
$b2  = random(-4, 4);
$b3  = random(-4, 4);

$ans = ParametricLine("<$b1,0,$b2,$b3>+t<-$a12,1,0,0>");

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [ ['There is no solution.'], [ 'The solution is %s', $ans ] ], 1);

# Now begin with the Problem Statement

BEGIN_PGML

Consider the following matrix in reduced row echelon form:

[```
\left[
\begin{array}{rrrr|r}
1 & [$a12] & 0 & 0 & [$b1] \\
0 & 0    & 1 & 0 & [$b2]\\
0 & 0    & 0 & 1 & [$b3] \\
\end{array}
\right] ```]

[_]{$rma}

Write the solution to the associated linear system in vector form using [` s`] or [`t`] as free variables if necessary.  For example use [|<1,2,3>+t<4,5,6>|]* or 
[|<1,2,3>+t<4,5,6>+s<7,8,9>|]*.
END_PGML

$eqn1 = Formula("$b1-$a12 y")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
In this case, there is one free variables, so [`y=t`]. The three rows can be written as the equations 
[``` \begin{aligned}
x & = [$eqn1] \\
z & = [$b2] \\
w & = [$b3]
\end{aligned}
```]
Writing the equations with the free variable and in vector form, the answer is
[``` [$ans] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
